  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Math\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Math\n       Program: commons-math\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/Math.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-math.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 106\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Math-73\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\nf6dd42b4fc01d1bef5392b6f19b6bcbafee27637\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2010-02-23 21:01:38 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nMATH-343\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MATH-343\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.math.analysis.solvers.BrentSolverTest::testBadEndpoints\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: Expecting IllegalArgumentException - non-bracketing\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.math.analysis.solvers.BrentSolver\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Brent solver doesn't throw IllegalArgumentException when initial guess has the wrong sign\nType: Bug | Priority: Critical | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nJavadoc for \"public double solve(final UnivariateRealFunction f, final double min, final double max, final double initial)\" claims that \"if the values of the function at the three points have the same sign\" an IllegalArgumentException is thrown. This case isn't even checked.\n\nComments:\n\n[Luc Maisonobe]: Fixed in subversion repository as of r915517\nThanks for reporting the issue\n\n[Volkan Aktas]: Thanks for the quick turnaround. One comment: I'm not sure whether the check before throwing the IllegalArgumentException is necessary. You can have only the following situations (given that min <= initial <= max and assuming neither min nor max is a root):\n\n    * yMin and yMax have the same sign:\n        ** yInitial has a different sign: Handled on line 121 (function is not monotonous between min and max)\n        ** yInitial has the same sign: Falls through to line 136 and yMin * yMax > 0 by definition\n    * yMin and yMax do not have the same sign:\n        ** yInitial has the same sign as yMax: Handled on line 121\n        ** yInitial has the same sign as yMin: Handled on line 133\n\nIn this case I'd say code between lines 131 and 142 should be replaced by the throw statement on line 137.\n\n[Luc Maisonobe]: You are right.\nI have removed the unreachable code and committed it in the subversion repository\nThanks again",
  "fix_diff": ""
}